 "heartbeat regulation" is to be scrapped and women are to be better protected against violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: Rights groups sound alarm over proposed anti-terror law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d3633bc124e5f5d15d5f6def6f963f141c0a36c08f612c45dcc35717e638115</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227--abd4d2b11674.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sri-lanka-rights-groups-sound-alarm-over-proposed-anti-terror-law/a-79932227?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sri Lankan government is looking to replace a controversial anti-terror law but critics say the new one is just as bad.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK court convicts 2 Iranian men of spying on journalists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c2f40e44478f5f8179ff53a36594e616ab27805d672985fd062fb6a482ec258</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583--9da85f420d5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has found two Iranian citizens guilty of surveilling reporters for a Persian-language television station critical of Iran's government. One was also convicted of planning a violent attack against them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Impeachment: How it works and why Trump should be worried</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3560b76a5279519cb3bf8c7ec89237ddb01abfecd0faf7250c92f5e0bcae90fb</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/impeachment-how-it-works-and-why-trump-should-be-worried/a-79931040--faa8753db476.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/impeachment-how-it-works-and-why-trump-should-be-worried/a-79931040?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pete Hegseth, Bill Clinton and Donald Trump (twice so far): attempts to impeach political figures are becoming common. The failure rate looks high, but according to experts, conviction is not always the aim.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, second affair leaves Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:354f94f00f9901f54cc5b85d9793b049c813628d8ba82335b231159e1e79937e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-second-affair-leaves-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--471686cc8872.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-second-affair-leaves-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO after a second affair came to light. DW examines how losing its figurehead will affect the firm and the US-China AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Exiled journalists still repressed by regime</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46aa68e1a5c4ffdf719f10c7f57eb10d941e36a2ebc80210d55050726901cbf9</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694--82c71d3aa718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-exiled-journalists-still-repressed-by-regime/a-79929694?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For many independent reporters, leaving Iran does not mean fully escaping the grasp of the Iranian state. The regime uses family members, bank accounts and the property they left behind to apply pressure across borders.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China's Xi Jinping renews calls for 'reunification' with Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f87fa396344d38c4a2e92d44a532ebb3a7fd106a0e16c547712774df11b38d77</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738--c3c1f561b896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-xi-jinping-renews-calls-for-reunification-with-taiwan/a-79929738?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping said that reunification was inevitable, but stopped short of mentioning military force. Taiwan though swiftly rejected Beijing's demands as tensions continue over the island's future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What are fossil fuels?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d57df1e73214f2e4420f4bef981bca8b7482043ad4697e49533700eff2a2f85</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540--1920eabf4714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">They are in our shampoo bottles, power our cars and heat our homes. But what actually are fossil fuels, and why do they matter?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Israel strikes Gaza hospital, says Hamas senior figure inside</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21e06726de14f86b171e2480f090509ec8ab560d9649d906bce749f6e137457c</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-strikes-gaza-hospital-says-hamas-senior-figure-inside/a-79927645--35a0867b6650.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-strikes-gaza-hospital-says-hamas-senior-figure-inside/a-79927645?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israel says Hamas was using the hospital as a military command center, while Palestinian officials report at least six people killed, including a surgeon. The strike comes amid an increasingly fragile ceasefire.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police raid chapters of Gremium MC biker gang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e320d6f87c8e3151d1d4b950acaadef52c1f8ea98fd7ea06139be3db321eb27</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T09:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-chapters-of-gremium-mc-biker-gang/live-79926275--65b7228f3ec1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-chapters-of-gremium-mc-biker-gang/live-79926275?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in southwestern Germany launched major early-morning operations against a biker gang. The state of Baden-Württemberg is outlawing three of its chapters. Meanwhile, unions are planning more strikes. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australian teen found alive after six days in the bush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6c05d153a02b6a03e051a26f205dd858ea44656a30cf394b24e00e3e6b7e100</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australian-teen-found-alive-after-six-days-in-the-bush/a-79926046--79cdcc67ba58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australian-teen-found-alive-after-six-days-in-the-bush/a-79926046?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The teenager was spotted during an aerial search, after spending days navigating rugged terrain. He had fallen down the side of a riverbed two days before being found.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bundeswehr study exposes widespread sexual harassment in German military</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e812f9d93c3b62efc51ff7ea075a5e636d5827194138517044cc1f1ffc8c8c8d</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundeswehr-study-exposes-widespread-sexual-harassment-in-german-military/a-79926359--0cec81791758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundeswehr-study-exposes-widespread-sexual-harassment-in-german-military/a-79926359?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sexual misconduct in the Bundeswehr is far more widespread than previously known, with younger women disproportionately affected. Defense Minister Boris Pistorius has called for a policy of "zero tolerance."</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Intelligent women get less help at work, study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:867a09a34a0706aae7e6281849c831621b8c44aab01fe5e1d9a9c2886fcfdd7c</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881--d3f9551f1647.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women who scored high on intelligence tests were seen as more hostile by their teammates and got less help, a new study finds. High-scoring men faced no such penalty. Research explains why.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Ind